<!-- ================================================================ TRUST -->
<section class="band" id="trust" aria-labelledby="trust-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · Trust &amp; security</span>
      <h2 id="trust-heading">Built to be <span class="accent">provable,</span> not just careful.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="two reveal">
      <div class="tlist">
        <div class="trow"><span class="mk">◇</span><div>
          <h3>Fail-closed policy</h3>
          <p>An unknown node, a sensitive input, a deceptive label — denied by default, before a human ever sees it.</p></div></div>
        <div class="trow"><span class="mk">◇</span><div>
          <h3>Safe component vocabulary</h3>
          <p>Agents compose from a constrained set of components. No raw model-authored HTML or scripts ever reach the DOM.</p></div></div>
        <div class="trow"><span class="mk">◇</span><div>
          <h3>Tamper-evident audit</h3>
          <p>A keyed, hash-chained log with a head anchor — interior edits and tail truncation are both detectable.</p></div></div>
        <div class="trow"><span class="mk">◇</span><div>
          <h3>Sandbox spectrum</h3>
          <p>Tool execution scales from native confinement to microVMs, with SSRF and egress guards on by default.</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="panel"><span class="c"># policy verdict — a generated login frame</span>
frame  <span class="h">uif-9c1a</span>
node   input[type=<span class="x">password</span>]
rule   <span class="x">sensitive_input</span>
<span class="x">✕ BLOCKED</span> — never rendered
audit  <span class="p">sha256</span>:1a2f9c… <span class="c">(recorded)</span>

<span class="c"># a safe frame, same pipeline</span>
frame  <span class="h">uif-4b7e</span>
<span class="o">✓ ALLOW</span> → human decision
resume <span class="o">durable ✓</span></div>
        <div class="badge-honest">
          <span class="mk">▲</span>
          <p><b>We mark shipped vs. roadmap plainly.</b> GA ships as a single-node
            appliance; the distributed multi-replica scheduler is tested library
            code, not yet in the binary. For a security product, candor is the point.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

